Mutation
- [N139] Node-level mutation: element=action(n6,"voluntary redundancy accepted"); source=i6:check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy; reason=The model changes an active instruction to check a condition into an assertion that the redundancy has already been accepted.
- [N140] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b7,c4,"v7 = 'No'"); source=i29:If the assessment is not satisfactory -> i30:the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted; reason=The guard routes the negative assessment path directly to a converge node, bypassing the required action to contact the next candidate on the shortlist.
- [N141] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b9,e4,"v9 = 'No'"); source=i41:Otherwise, if the candidate accepts; reason=The source text indicates the process continues upon this condition, but the model incorrectly routes it to an end node.
- [N142] Node-level mutation: element=guard(b10,e5,"v10 = 'Yes'"); source=i42:If the renegotiation is successful; reason=The source text indicates the process continues upon successful renegotiation, but the model incorrectly routes it to an end node.
